From 8f07becc235b818867acb234b4ec586ac98310fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:50:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] feat(asks): a per-person answer record by field (1689,
 A6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Outcomes were recorded per search and per goal, never per person asked, so
the engine could not tell who answers about what, how fast, or who helps.

- Migration 217: answer_stats(user_id, field, asked, yes, no, referred,
  later, silent, first_answer_minutes_median, helped, bridged, updated_at),
  separate counters, no merged score.
- Recounted from the source tables (task_asks, outcome_events „worked" on
  the ask, accepted introductions as the go-between) — never incremented,
  so it cannot drift: right after a first ask, after an answer or decline,
  after a „helped" debrief, and an hourly sweep for everything else.
- Each first ask is filed under its field (the goal's first field words;
  the empty field when it names none). `referred` stays 0 until A13.
- Read only on the admin per-user page (answerStats block); never in any
  user's app, never in a run.

DONE WHEN: after one ask answered yes and one declined on fictional seats,
the two records show the right counters and the median minutes; a debrief
„helped" adds 1 to helped; the numbers appear nowhere in any user's app.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
